<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Sixteenth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 BCE – 1580 BCE (approx.) · capital Thebes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Theban dynasty of the Second Intermediate Period that held Upper Egypt against the Hyksos.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the Thirteenth Dynasty collapsed and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Hyksos</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/memphis-egypt">Memphis</a> around 1650 BCE, a line of kings established itself at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>, controlling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/abydos">Abydos</a> to Elephantine. Its existence as a separate dynasty was clarified by the reconstruction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin-king-list">Turin King List</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kim-ryholt">Kim Ryholt</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kings ruled a small, embattled realm, and their stelae speak of war and famine. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neferhotep-iii">Neferhotep III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebiryraw-i">Nebiryraw I</a> are among the better-attested rulers; stelae of Neferhotep III boast of rescuing <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> in a time of hunger. They relied on the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a> and local garrisons, and were pressed by both the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Fifteenth Dynasty of Egypt</a> to the north and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kerma">Kerma</a> to the south.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1580 BCE the line seems to have been overrun by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Hyksos</a> campaigns or replaced from within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a>, and it was followed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/seventeenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Seventeenth Dynasty of Egypt</a>, which led the war of liberation.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sixteenth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Sixteenth Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="653"><figcaption>Image: Iry-Hor · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egypt_Hyksos_Period.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 BCE – 1580 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century-bce">17th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thebes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Neferhotep III, Nebiryraw I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sixteenth Dynasty, Theban Sixteenth Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1615&amp;focus=sixteenth-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Sixteenth Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5543 1232 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sixteenth Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5863 1488L5813 1353M5863 1488L5863 1488"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5813 1353h0M5863 1488h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5863 1488h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5863 1488h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thebes. <a href="/atlas?year=-1615&amp;focus=sixteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
